"Then we moved online, and every platform asked for a piece of you - your name, your number, your friends. We accepted that the price of talking to others is letting someone know who we talk to. Every generation, people and tech, had it this way - telephone, email, messengers, social media. It seemed the only way possible." = "然後我們轉向線上，每個平台都要求你提供一些信息--你的姓名、電話號碼、好友列表。我們接受了這樣一個事實：與人交流的代價就是讓別人知道我們在和誰交流。每一代人，每一代科技，都遵循着這樣的模式--電話、電子郵件、即時通訊、社交媒體。這似乎是唯一可行的方式。";

/* No comment provided by engineer. */
"There is another way. A network with no phone numbers. No usernames. No accounts. No user identities of any kind. A network that connects people and carries encrypted messages without knowing who is connected." = "還有另一種方法。一個沒有電話號碼、沒有使用者名、沒有賬户、沒有任何使用者身分的網絡。一個連接人們並傳輸加密信息的網絡，而無需知道誰連接了。";

